# Storefront logo size

Every creator subdomain uses the same header logo sizes. Do not size logos per store (`maxfreedom`, `filialsons`, or any other host). Do not add subdomain checks or one-off CSS to make a mark larger.

Display caps (maximum, not a target to grow past):

- Wordmark (horizontal custom): **32px** tall on desktop, **24px** tall on mobile (`max-width: 768px`)
- Square/round custom: **82px** on desktop, **70×56px** on mobile

Keep these in `frontend/src/Components/Navbar/Navbar.css` on `.logo--custom.logo--horizontal` and `.logo--custom.logo--square`. Do not raise `height`, `max-height`, `width`, or `max-width` on those rules.

Trim empty canvas so a padded PNG still fills these caps instead of looking tiny. Do not scale a mark above the caps to compensate for padding.

ScreenMerch.com’s own mug/square logo is separate. Do not copy its 160px/82px header sizes onto custom storefront wordmarks.
